==Enemy==
Angelic Beast Rajakong looks like a combination of [[Angelic Gory]] and [[Ragin' Gory]], but has more than 3 times as much health as both of them combined. He's immune to both [[Wave Attack|Waves]] and [[Surge Attack|Surges]], has 50 Omni Strike piercing range and a 10% chance for a Lv. 2 Wave on every hit, dealing double damage at close quarters and hurting an area of 667.5 range.

==Strategy==
You absolutely want [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] as your meatshield due to Rajakong's insane pushing power and speed. Be attentive in battle and look out for incoming enemies that may quickly whittle down Ramen Cat and allow Rajakong to suddenly push. As such, [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]] serves as great protection for your existing stack in times of need, along with the [[Ototo Corps|Slow Beam]] and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]].

[[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]] with Tough Vs and Target Angel [[Talents]] can help to push him back, especially if he can also hinder supporting enemies greatly. Though whenever Rajakong is left vulnerable to attacks, it is advisable to not use Fiend Cat and to instead maximize damage dealt onto him. [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] with the Wave Immunity Talent unlocked can cripple him, but she tends to miss often due to Rajakong's high knockback count, depending on the given stage and your lineup.

For damage, either [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune cats]] or cats with low knockback counts should be used due to Rajakong's frequent Wave Attacks and range. Talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] is a good option, especially when you get a stack of them going off. However, out of many of the non-Uber options, the best of all is [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] (which usually isn't obtained until after at least one Rajakong encounter), with Behemoth Slayer, Massive Damage to Angels and Wave immunity with longer range than Rajakong's Omni Strike to effectively counter him with little to no hassle, similarly to how [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] beats up [[Casaurian Ahirujo]], and [[Lifeguard Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Gelato Bro Cats]] can be a solid option for additional Wave-Immune DPS with the addition of Behemoth Slayer in their [[True Form]].

In tight situations, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] is a great backup option to chip off sizeable amounts of health, but it can be inconsistent due to Rajakong's Waves and Omni Strike. When building your lineup, you should only consider [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] if it consists of a substantial number of units that can turn the tides of battle yet are vulnerable to Rajakong's Wave Attacks (like Awakened Bahamut Cat), as Rajakong can quickly shred through casual usage of Octopus Cat.

